# BioSketch3D frontend environment example
#
# No IP address configuration is required for the same-Wi-Fi QR workflow.
#
# Start Vite with:
#   npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0
#
# Open the Vite Network URL printed in the terminal, for example:
#   http://192.168.1.10:5173/
#
# The frontend automatically uses the same hostname for the backend:
#   http://192.168.1.10:8000
#
# Keep this example file in GitHub as documentation.
# Do not create frontend/.env unless you later add a separate optional setting.
